From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 18:16:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] media: qcom: camss: csiphy: take the settle rate from the
 timer clock

csiphy_set_clock_rates() stores the rate of every clock it rates in
csiphy->timer_clk_rate, so the value that ends up feeding
csiphy_settle_cnt_calc() is whichever rated clock happens to come last in
the resource table.

That was harmless while the settle timer was the only rated clock, but it
stops being true as soon as a PHY also rates its own core clock - which
the v5.x parts have to, since they cannot sample a high speed link off the
power-on default. The settle count then silently shifts, and a settle
count that is too short is a link that never locks, reported four stages
downstream as a VFE SOF timeout.

Only assign timer_clk_rate for the csiphyN_timer clock, and program each
clock with its own rounded rate.

Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 .../media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csiphy.c  | 33 ++++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csiphy.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csiphy.c
index 2de97f58f9ae..f0a191137e53 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csiphy.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csiphy.c
@@ -130,6 +130,15 @@ static u8 csiphy_get_bpp(const struct csiphy_format_info *formats,
 	return formats[0].bpp;
 }
 
+static bool csiphy_match_clock_name(const char *clock_name, const char *format,
+				    int index)
+{
+	char name[16]; /* csiphyXXX_timer\0 */
+
+	snprintf(name, sizeof(name), format, index);
+	return !strcmp(clock_name, name);
+}
+
 /*
  * csiphy_set_clock_rates - Calculate and set clock rates on CSIPHY module
  * @csiphy: CSIPHY device
@@ -180,9 +189,18 @@ static int csiphy_set_clock_rates(struct csiphy_device *csiphy)
 				return -EINVAL;
 			}
 
-			csiphy->timer_clk_rate = round_rate;
-
-			ret = clk_set_rate(clock->clk, csiphy->timer_clk_rate);
+			/*
+			 * Only the timer clock drives the settle counter.
+			 * A CSIPHY may have more than one rated clock - the
+			 * v5.x PHYs also rate their own core clock - and
+			 * taking the rate of whichever came last silently
+			 * skews every settle count derived from it.
+			 */
+			if (csiphy_match_clock_name(clock->name, "csiphy%d_timer",
+						    csiphy->id))
+				csiphy->timer_clk_rate = round_rate;
+
+			ret = clk_set_rate(clock->clk, round_rate);
 			if (ret < 0) {
 				dev_err(dev, "clk set rate failed: %d\n", ret);
 				return ret;
@@ -558,15 +576,6 @@ static int csiphy_init_formats(struct v4l2_subdev *sd,
 	return csiphy_set_format(sd, fh ? fh->state : NULL, &format);
 }
 
-static bool csiphy_match_clock_name(const char *clock_name, const char *format,
-				    int index)
-{
-	char name[16]; /* csiphyXXX_timer\0 */
-
-	snprintf(name, sizeof(name), format, index);
-	return !strcmp(clock_name, name);
-}
-
 /*
  * msm_csiphy_subdev_init - Initialize CSIPHY device structure and resources
  * @csiphy: CSIPHY device
